WEBVTT

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.490
What are you guys?!

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.580
It's a holy object.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.900
What are you saying?!

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.210
Die to repay your sins!

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.250
No!

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:48.040
My morning starts with safe, worry-free, synthetic food from SVC.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.100
It might sound unbelievable now,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.070
but it's said that in the past,
humans killed and ate other creatures.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:13.670
That's a tale from thirty years ago,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.090
when the System of Society was barbaric and still developing.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.100
The System of Society protects us,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:25.960
and we grow up to become adults who protect the System.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.990
But...

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:35.560
what happens if we can't become adults?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.600
Have you made contact with your friends from the new group?

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.700
No, not yet.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:50.070
In the modern age, where Monitor Education has become the norm,

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:56.070
students like you who resist Real Communication aren't rare.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:59.030
Is that so?

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.980
It's because more children are living alone.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:12.900
That's why counselors like me are assigned to community centers to guide you.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.560
I see.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.670
First, make Real Contact with the kids from the new group.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.410
From there, we'll spread the circle continuously.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.180
I didn't really feel anything after I was told that.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.190
The world in the frame is the world I know.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.300
The sky, the sea...

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.070
all seem artificial.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.620
The real world...

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.280
Even though this world seems more real.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:52.460
Kono-san...

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.280
Kono Ayumi-san:

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.730
a girl who transferred to a nearby Center this spring.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.180
Although she should've been in the same group as me,

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.430
she was in a different world.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.680
I felt that way somehow.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.310
Makino!

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.180
What are you up to?

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.690
U-Um...

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.920
Tsuzuki-san?

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:18.940
Right!

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:23.600
I'm Tsuzuki Mio-sama, the genius who was assigned to the same Group 21 as you!

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.340
Nice to meet you!

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.260
N-Nice to meet you.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.620
So, what were you doing?

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.830
Oh, it's Kono.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.330
You're spying on her?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.770
N-No!

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.210
Hey, Kono!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.970
Come here!

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.080
Makino is spying on you!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.190
Makino, do you love me?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.940
Or are you keeping watch over me?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.420
That's...

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.740
Keeping watch? That's not nice to say.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.980
Really?

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.840
We are being watched, after all...

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.980
by that machine.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.370
The Image Collection Device.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:17.280
Throughout the city, the System has eyes that watch us constantly.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.590
We've become used to it.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:25.930
I hate others taking more of an interest in me than necessary.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.840
So then, I'd like to get straight to the main topic.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.800
A corpse has been found in Area 122.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.950
We received a report from the Prefecture Police

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:42.610
that the victim, Kawabata Ryuga, is a student at our Center.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:47.060
The police are asking for our full cooperation in the investigation.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.640
Our Center will conform to their requirements.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.210
Does anyone object to this?

00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:01.090
Now, please be prompt, and for each student that you counselors manage,

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.990
send in a detailed copy of their data.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.650
What's the matter, Fuwa Shizue-kun?

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.050
It's against office regulations

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:17.980
to release student data to a third party without the consent of the students and their guardians.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.370
Fuwa-kun, this is, you see...

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.950
We are taking measures beyond the law.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.410
Who are you?

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.350
Prefecture Police Detective Department, R-Investigation Section,

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:35.760
Lead Administrative Officer for
Atrocious Crimes, Ishida Riichiro.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.040
This is about the murder case that happened in Area 122.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.160
In the victim's action and communication logs,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:52.180
we found many entries related to deformed characters.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.040
The investigation headquarters has decided

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.890
that the victim's acquaintances with similar interests...

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.550
will be the starting point for the investigation.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:05.440
Please cooperate with us.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.060
Anything I tell them is meaningless.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.010
Totally meaningless.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.590
Ishida is the great-grandchild of the SVC's founder.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.760
Some city authority like him decided this.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.250
No one can resist.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.290
Kunugi-san...

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.510
Why are you here?

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.240
I came to put the data...

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:36.790
onto the specified media—

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.480
Oh, where did it go?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:44.320
Sign: R Prefecture Police 02

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.800
The order was to copy the records.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:48.360
So you didn't come to see me.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.670
I'm sorry for leaving you alone for a week.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.040
I've been assigned as lead investigator in this area, starting today.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:03.000
I never imagined I'd be involved in a serial murder case again.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:05.400
Oh, sorry.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.960
I must've reminded you about your mother.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:13.400
Don't think of me and my mother as the same.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.260
m 0 0 l 290 0 290 350 0 350

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.260
16-year-old serial killer

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:17.890
Although she was counseling a suspected serial killer,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.930
why would they try to commit suicide together?

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:26.230
Kunugi-san?

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:30.990
Don't badmouth people who have passed away.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:35.740
I was assigned to that incident too,
and in the end, that was the conclusion.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.120
I feel ashamed of myself.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:45.460
So you were talking about a copy of the data.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:49.460
Yeah.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.730
How was the Center?

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:07.430
Well, I was able to talk with friends today.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.010
That's nice to hear.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:10.630
I'm happy too.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.660
Is anything wrong, Hazuki-san?

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:18.620
Um...

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.580
When will you come see me again?

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.420
We have a National Assembly this month.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:27.290
I'll come Wednesday of next month, as scheduled.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.290
Is anything wrong?

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.510
No.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.950
Well, Hazuki-san, we heard that dangerous incidents were occurring,

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.490
so get some rest after you've secured the house.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.790
Okay.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.750
Good night, Father.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.200
Good night.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.150
He probably won't come next month either.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.550
Wh-What?!

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.510
Someone is here!

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:22.690
Who is it?

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:36.780
Yo!

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.050
Tsuzuki-san?

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.090
How did you get in?

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:42.660
I used magic.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.750
Magic?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.430
Yeah, magic.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:49.710
Oh yeah, by the way, that—

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.780
What? Me?

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:54.040
Not you. Behind you.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.790
The Monitor?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:59.750
Turn on the Image Collection Device for this room.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.950
Okay.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.640
Huh?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.600
Why?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.560
Why aren't you visible on it?

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.290
In this world where people rely on the System for everything,

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:18.150
I'm the equivalent of a magician. I can do whatever I want.

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:19.900
That's how it is.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.110
Why are you in my house?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.290
That's because...

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.410
Look at that.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:27.280
The home Monitor?

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.870
Music, start!

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.820
What's that?

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.380
I was thinking of doing that for the group training assignment.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:49.890
We should discuss it during the noon training session.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.730
Email is fine too.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:54.820
It's for communication, you know?

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:58.590
Also, Yabe was absent today, right?

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:02.530
So I went to her home to talk to her directly.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.740
It looks like the police are after her.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.270
The police are searching for Yabe-san?

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:12.680
Yeah, so I thought we should look for her.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.710
Why?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.170
Because we're friends, of course.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.420
Friends?

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.380
Let's go!

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.340
You're friends too, right?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.310
Y-Yes.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.080
Okay, it's decided.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.260
For starters, we'll go to Kono's place.

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:31.210
What?

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:32.780
To Kono-san's place?

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.220
Tsuzuki-san!

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.930
Oh right, the Monitor.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:46.790
Thirty seconds.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:47.830
Thirty seconds?

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.300
That's when the magic spell will begin to affect you.

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:54.630
We'll become invisible during that time.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.630
A blackout?

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.700
The magic is starting to take effect.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:01.210
Really?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.510
It's going to begin now.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:03.610
Begin?

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.660
We're out of time.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:07.430
Out of time?

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:13.560
Tsuzuki-san, what's going to—

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.350
I'm going now.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.150
Oh, wait!

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.330
Is it okay?

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.350
The limitation with this magic is that it can fool the mechanical eyes,

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.200
but it can't fool human eyes.

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:43.990
It's okay. Come out.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:48.670
If you wanted information about the Area Patrol, you could've just checked the GPS.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.970
H-Huh?

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.270
We can't use the Monitors.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.070
Because of the magic.

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:59.230
They could track where we are if we used the Monitors.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.260
Oh, you're right.

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:01.400
Yep!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.740
Everything has to be experienced firsthand.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:06.530
Let's go.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.810
O-Okay.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:13.170
Aren't you worried about getting lost without GPS?

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.000
It's fine.

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:19.500
We're not following some route that the System chose.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.880
The destination is the result of moving in the direction you feel like going.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:29.590
That's why we're walking now, heading for Kono's house.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.190
I guess...

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:36.370
Here?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:37.020
Right.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.910
Kono-san seems to be absent.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:44.100
Is she out somewhere?

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:48.270
How odd of her to be out so late.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:49.950
That goes for us too, you kno—

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.690
Tsuzuki-san!

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.600
Hey!

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.270
Don't leave me here!

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.280
Hey!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.880
I'm going up first.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.070
Up?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.750
Kono-san...

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.760
What can you see from there?

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.220
The sky.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.710
There's nothing.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:01.250
Having nothing, and being invisible...

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.390
That's a philosophical way of thinking.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.860
Did you come here to discuss philosophy?

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:10.040
Nope.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.730
I came to discuss the performance we have to do for training.

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:15.010
With a vigilant eye...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.830
I was thinking of doing this PV.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.430
Just for that?

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.800
And you came along too, Makino?

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.620
Oh, I'm...

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.120
I think Makino wanted to see you.

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:43.490
Try communicating.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:44.480
What happened to Yabe?

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.440
Yabe?

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.680
I stopped by her place.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:52.400
She wasn't there, and the police were accessing her home Monitor log.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:55.550
Also, Sakura Hinako from the same class,

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:58.540
and someone I don't know named Nakamura, were accessing it too.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.370
The police, huh?

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:03.580
That's worrying.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.530
What are you calling worrying?

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:09.020
What are we going to do if Yabe is involved in an incident?

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:11.540
Incident?

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:14.010
You mean Yabe-san isn't <i>just</i> missing?

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.080
It's a possibility.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.690
You've heard about the serial killings, right?

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:20.300
Yeah.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.530
Do you know who got killed?

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.940
Was it Yabe-san, perhaps?

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:28.900
Yabe isn't dead.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:31.600
Right, she isn't dead.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:33.360
He's the one that died.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:35.440
Who?

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.000
Come here.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.120
O-Okay.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.540
Kawabata Ryu, age 16.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.420
Who?

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.500
A boy in Wednesday's class.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.170
So it wasn't Yabe-san.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:53.240
Where did you get this data?

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:56.260
From the storage server at D&S that does area security.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:17:59.560
Hacking?

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:01.110
Who knows?

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:02.740
That's illegal.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.230
Don't you agree, Makino?

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:12.570
You don't have to act that surprised just because you have a problem communicating.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.430
I-I'm sorry!

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:18.570
Kono, you should be more considerate too.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.190
You've read your friends' profiles, right?

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:22.610
I haven't.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:25.830
I hate having relationships with other people.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:30.380
But still, it's amazing that you knew Yabe wasn't dead.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:33.270
That's classified information, you know.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.380
"That"?

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.620
I had Real Contact with the kid who died.

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:40.600
You mean you met Kawabata?

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.310
Three nights ago,

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.920
I just happened to see him.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:48.690
I often leave the house when it gets dark.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.270
It was the same that time too.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:56.350
Kawabata seemed to be chasing Yabe, without success.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:58.810
"Seemed"?

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:00.740
And you didn't save her?

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.950
I was merely observing.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.070
Because my route home goes the same way,

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:10.620
I ended up following them.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:14.880
Then another person wearing a mask appeared.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.430
They were able to corner Yabe.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.270
So you finally saved her?

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.800
I didn't save her.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.730
Someone else did.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:43.490
Damn you!

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:56.760
Myao?

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:58.150
Myao?

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:02.720
She had long hair and was wearing clothes like they wear on the continent, right?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.270
That's right.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:05.930
She was using strange techniques too.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.200
Then there's no doubt.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:10.400
Myao saved Yabe.

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:11.400
Rei Myao.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:15.110
Then Yabe-san is with Myao-san?

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:16.820
You're probably correct.

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.460
All right.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.680
Let's go meet Myao now.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:21.780
Now?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.720
Yabe might be in trouble, you know?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.320
We're her friends, so we should go save her.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:30.310
I have something I want to ask this Myao person too.

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:31.570
I'm coming.

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.400
You're coming too, right, Makino?

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.440
Y-Yes.

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:43.920
We weren't given any notice about providing personal information.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:49.010
I only heard today what I was supposed to do.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:49.680
Oh?

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:52.900
A copy error?

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.410
The data cannot be collected?

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:57.270
Is the data corrupt?

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.950
There shouldn't be any problem with the data itself.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:07.950
No Monitor exists.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:09.790
Who is she?

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:11.740
Yabe Yuko.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.500
She's a student I'm in charge of.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.110
She should've been absent today.

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.440
There should be a GPS on the Monitor.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:19.210
What's the log show?

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:21.670
The final log entry is...

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.290
Area C.

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:27.660
Area C?

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:31.700
That's not all. Area C is the crime scene from this morning.

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:34.870
Prefecture Police Headquarters, Koizumi here.

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:37.040
First Investigation Section Group Three, Kunugi here.

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:40.000
Get me the security records from the home of the person whose ID I'm sending.

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:49.300
She hasn't returned home for three days.

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.340
Her visitors were...

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:53.740
Sakura Hinako and Nakamura Yuji.

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:58.730
I don't know about Nakamura-san, but Sakura-san is my student.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:06.090
Nakamura Yuji is an important witness, who is now a suspect in the killings.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.200
We're pursuing him.

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:10.910
A suspect...

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:12.640
Don't tell me, Yabe-san is also—

00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:14.830
I don't know.

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:18.620
But Nakamura is somewhere in this town.

00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:38.470
Is this Area C?

00:22:38.470 --> 00:22:39.420
That's right.

00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:41.090
Are you scared?

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:44.320
I'm not scared, but isn't it dangerous?

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:46.010
Since it's a designated redevelopment area,

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:49.620
and the old city just left it like this, I wouldn't say it's completely safe.

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:52.140
But security robots still patrol the area.

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:56.480
Are you surprised that I'm living here?

00:22:58.060 --> 00:22:59.950
Y-Yes.

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:01.720
What an honest girl.

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:04.370
It's me!

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:07.730
Is someone in there?

00:23:07.730 --> 00:23:09.220
It's voice recognition.

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:11.640
We're free to modify things here.

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:12.680
Come on in.

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:29.010
No need to be shy!

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:31.010
Come this way!

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.640
So then...

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.350
This is the main module of my Monitor.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:38.570
This is your Monitor?

00:23:38.570 --> 00:23:41.220
That's a Monitor too,

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:46.520
but it's only the name of a terminal that has data harvesting capabilities.

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:50.700
The word Monitor originally meant "to watch."

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:53.200
There are Image Collection Devices placed throughout the city,

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:57.040
and security robots patrol the places without Image Collection Devices.

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:00.000
They're actually monitoring our every move.

00:24:00.810 --> 00:24:04.210
While we have Monitors that double as monitoring devices,

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.450
we're also being constantly monitored.

00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:12.730
But I say "no thanks" to being monitored.

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:14.640
So...

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:20.370
I'll monitor them back.

00:24:22.130 --> 00:24:24.250
What are you hoping to do by monitoring them?

00:24:24.250 --> 00:24:27.860
Well, if I don't like it...

00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:33.660
I'll destroy everything.

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:36.290
Are you going to use a bomb or something?

00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:39.510
Look behind you.

00:24:42.100 --> 00:24:44.320
What is that?

00:24:44.320 --> 00:24:45.710
Turtle-1.

00:24:46.030 --> 00:24:47.630
A plasma generating device.

00:24:48.220 --> 00:24:51.260
If I activate it, the area around this place will go...

00:24:53.990 --> 00:24:57.180
kaboom!

00:25:02.020 --> 00:25:03.560
Just kidding.

00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:06.170
If you do that...

00:25:06.170 --> 00:25:07.520
...you'll be caught by the police.

00:25:08.410 --> 00:25:09.990
Of course I won't be caught.

00:25:10.550 --> 00:25:13.890
From here, we can see everything in this world.

00:25:13.890 --> 00:25:15.460
So here.

00:25:16.940 --> 00:25:19.150
We can see where Myao is too.

00:25:24.810 --> 00:25:26.540
I'll ask again.

00:25:26.810 --> 00:25:29.090
Was it you who sold off my friends?

00:25:58.360 --> 00:25:59.500
Myao!

00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:01.430
Long time no see.

00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:03.330
You're amazing, as usual.

00:26:04.760 --> 00:26:07.170
You beat them up all by yourself?

00:26:07.720 --> 00:26:09.880
That has nothing to do with you.

00:26:11.590 --> 00:26:13.700
It's between you and me.

00:26:14.910 --> 00:26:17.490
Don't be such a stranger.

00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:18.670
Who are those two?

00:26:19.050 --> 00:26:19.800
Them?

00:26:21.940 --> 00:26:23.220
Kono and Makino.

00:26:23.220 --> 00:26:24.270
Huh?

00:26:24.270 --> 00:26:25.920
My friends.

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:30.790
Hey, do you know where to find a girl named Yabe?

00:26:30.790 --> 00:26:32.230
You saved her, right?

00:26:34.240 --> 00:26:36.940
If you want to know about that incident, you should ask <i>her.</i>

00:26:36.940 --> 00:26:38.060
Her?

00:26:38.660 --> 00:26:39.820
Kono?

00:26:43.180 --> 00:26:45.040
So you remember me.

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:48.280
I wouldn't forget.

00:26:48.280 --> 00:26:50.250
So you saved her after all.

00:26:50.380 --> 00:26:51.090
No!

00:26:53.070 --> 00:26:57.310
Sure, I protected that girl from your area.

00:26:57.310 --> 00:27:00.170
But <i>she's</i> the one that took them down.

00:27:00.170 --> 00:27:01.430
How strange.

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:05.860
You should've been unconscious and unable to see anything.

00:27:06.990 --> 00:27:09.330
Unconscious?

00:27:09.330 --> 00:27:10.400
Myao was?

00:27:11.480 --> 00:27:15.360
She definitely beat the attacker, Kawabata.

00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:16.290
But...

00:27:27.450 --> 00:27:28.760
That's it.

00:27:28.760 --> 00:27:30.480
That's it?

00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:31.960
Save Myao then!

00:27:32.820 --> 00:27:35.260
I don't know how to fight.

00:27:36.450 --> 00:27:37.310
And...

00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:41.640
I can't do something meaningless like hitting people.

00:27:41.880 --> 00:27:43.320
Did you say "meaningless"?

00:27:43.320 --> 00:27:45.600
Don't get so excited!

00:27:45.600 --> 00:27:47.810
Fight with me, and you'll see if it's meaningless!

00:27:47.810 --> 00:27:49.010
Hey, stop!

00:27:47.970 --> 00:27:49.500
That's meaningless too.

00:27:49.010 --> 00:27:50.100
Myao!

00:27:49.500 --> 00:27:51.620
It's meaningful to me!

00:27:53.650 --> 00:27:54.570
What?

00:27:56.420 --> 00:27:57.740
She woke up.

00:27:58.860 --> 00:28:00.670
Is there something upstairs?

00:28:01.270 --> 00:28:01.970
Yeah.

00:28:01.970 --> 00:28:03.270
Goods for sale.

00:28:03.830 --> 00:28:04.580
Goods for sale?

00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:06.490
I'm done playing with you guys.

00:28:06.490 --> 00:28:08.720
Hey, tell me!

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:09.840
You can watch and figure it out.

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:11.830
Fine, I'll go see with my very own eyes.

00:28:12.490 --> 00:28:13.550
Um...

00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:20.250
Kono-san, are you going too?

00:28:24.160 --> 00:28:26.260
Makino, what did you come here for?

00:28:28.730 --> 00:28:32.180
Well, Tsuzuki-san asked me, and...

00:28:32.180 --> 00:28:34.730
Tsuzuki came here to meet that Myao.

00:28:35.170 --> 00:28:38.640
I came here to ask Myao about Yabe.

00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:41.240
Neither of those things has anything to do with you.

00:28:44.170 --> 00:28:46.260
You should do what you want to do.

00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:50.360
Even if you ask me, I don't know what you want to do.

00:29:15.820 --> 00:29:20.360
Tsuzuki-san said... I can't use Monitors.

00:29:20.360 --> 00:29:22.170
It's because of the magic.

00:29:22.170 --> 00:29:25.310
They could track where we are if we used Monitors.

00:29:25.310 --> 00:29:26.360
Oh, you're right.

00:29:26.360 --> 00:29:27.340
Yep.

00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:30.830
Everything has to be experienced firsthand.

00:29:33.250 --> 00:29:34.750
You're friends too, right?

00:29:36.610 --> 00:29:37.960
Friends...

00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:40.670
Makino, what did you come here for?

00:30:01.600 --> 00:30:02.530
Goods for sale?

00:30:02.540 --> 00:30:05.050
Who would actually sell humans?

00:30:05.050 --> 00:30:08.450
There are some who buy people that aren't in the family register like me.

00:30:08.830 --> 00:30:09.710
Who would do that?

00:30:09.710 --> 00:30:10.990
I don't know.

00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:14.910
The people I beat up downstairs were only middlemen.

00:30:15.530 --> 00:30:17.960
So Yabe was a victim of it.

00:30:18.660 --> 00:30:20.090
Yabe-san?

00:30:20.090 --> 00:30:21.210
Yeah.

00:30:21.210 --> 00:30:22.880
Myao was protecting her.

00:30:23.270 --> 00:30:24.800
But she was kidnapped.

00:30:24.800 --> 00:30:26.290
Kidnapped?

00:30:26.290 --> 00:30:29.380
Everyone here in the attic was kidnapped as well.

00:30:31.340 --> 00:30:33.570
Everyone here?

00:30:33.570 --> 00:30:34.370
Yeah.

00:30:34.910 --> 00:30:35.940
Why?

00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:38.560
They're all unregistered people.

00:30:39.240 --> 00:30:41.690
If they never really existed, right from the beginning,

00:30:41.690 --> 00:30:43.950
the police won't do anything if they disappear.

00:30:44.680 --> 00:30:45.650
That's right.

00:30:45.890 --> 00:30:48.000
Yabe was a victim of that.

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:48.810
Right, Myao?

00:30:49.710 --> 00:30:50.830
Yeah.

00:31:11.940 --> 00:31:12.810
Hey!

00:31:13.970 --> 00:31:17.520
I couldn't leave her next to those dead bodies.

00:31:18.210 --> 00:31:19.830
Even though I took her back and protected her,

00:31:19.830 --> 00:31:21.230
she still ended up here.

00:31:21.760 --> 00:31:24.750
At least she was saved in the end.

00:31:24.750 --> 00:31:26.960
There's a problem though.

00:31:26.960 --> 00:31:27.950
A problem?

00:31:28.650 --> 00:31:31.770
If the person who attacked Yabe is still searching for her,

00:31:31.770 --> 00:31:34.400
it'll be dangerous to send her back home.

00:31:34.920 --> 00:31:37.640
Myao's place won't do, because she might be kidnapped again.

00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:38.870
We can't leave her there either.

00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:41.180
My place is in Area C.

00:31:41.180 --> 00:31:44.220
If something goes wrong, they'll use it as an excuse to do area re-planning.

00:31:44.220 --> 00:31:45.340
I can't let that happen.

00:31:45.750 --> 00:31:47.750
I won't let that happen!

00:31:47.750 --> 00:31:49.800
Your hard work is pointless.

00:31:49.800 --> 00:31:55.770
Anyway, Makino's place is literally made out of security, so we can't leave her there either.

00:31:55.770 --> 00:32:01.570
Is there anywhere that's safe like Area A,
but with more relaxed security?

00:32:06.160 --> 00:32:06.860
That's right!

00:32:15.250 --> 00:32:16.680
I suppose so.

00:32:25.150 --> 00:32:27.820
Thank you for hiding me.

00:32:28.380 --> 00:32:30.150
I feel bothered.

00:32:30.150 --> 00:32:32.010
Don't say that!

00:32:33.180 --> 00:32:35.100
Still, I'm bothering everyone, right?

00:32:35.100 --> 00:32:36.720
Forget about it.

00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:38.430
After all, we're friends.

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:40.770
Friends?

00:32:40.770 --> 00:32:41.900
For what?

00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:43.560
This!

00:32:44.830 --> 00:32:46.680
A stuffed animal?

00:32:46.680 --> 00:32:47.640
A stuffed animal, indeed.

00:32:47.640 --> 00:32:48.880
Yes, a stuffed animal.

00:32:48.880 --> 00:32:50.870
So a stuffed animal is your friend?

00:32:51.840 --> 00:32:53.160
That's not what I mean.

00:32:57.850 --> 00:32:58.770
This!

00:32:58.770 --> 00:33:00.430
Nope...

00:33:00.430 --> 00:33:01.870
Oh, this.

00:33:13.480 --> 00:33:14.620
Music?

00:33:15.710 --> 00:33:18.160
A girl band from long ago.

00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:23.320
The four of us have been doing some group training at the Center.

00:33:23.320 --> 00:33:25.110
With a vigilant eye!

00:33:25.910 --> 00:33:27.020
You try it too, Makino!

00:33:28.850 --> 00:33:30.570
Oh, um...

00:33:30.570 --> 00:33:31.490
With a vigilant...

00:33:31.490 --> 00:33:33.050
W-With a vigilant...

00:33:33.050 --> 00:33:34.000
...eye!

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:34.950
...eye?

00:33:34.950 --> 00:33:36.220
...eye!

00:33:37.070 --> 00:33:38.380
You too, Kono.

00:33:38.380 --> 00:33:40.300
I won't do it.

00:33:40.300 --> 00:33:41.370
What's wrong with you?!

00:33:42.270 --> 00:33:44.280
It's group training, you know.

00:33:44.280 --> 00:33:46.870
We have to do it together, or our grades will drop!

00:33:46.870 --> 00:33:48.970
You care about your grades?

00:33:48.970 --> 00:33:53.340
The stuff the adults give you is pointless.

00:33:50.550 --> 00:33:52.680
So you're rather enthusiastic, Makino?

00:33:52.680 --> 00:33:53.340
That's unexpected.

00:33:53.340 --> 00:33:54.890
I'm not like that at all.

00:33:54.320 --> 00:33:55.570
That's right.

00:33:54.890 --> 00:33:58.300
I have a communications disorder.

00:33:55.570 --> 00:33:57.310
We want to get a response from the audience.

00:33:57.310 --> 00:34:00.020
We're going to present this to other people at the Center.

00:34:00.020 --> 00:34:00.810
You're doing fine.

00:34:00.660 --> 00:34:02.960
It has to make an impression!

00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:09.800
You can leave performance tricks to people who do that for a living.

00:34:03.030 --> 00:34:06.350
You're communicating with me just fine right now.

00:34:07.210 --> 00:34:14.260
If not, they couldn't have brought you this far or be able to talk to you.

00:34:09.800 --> 00:34:12.200
But we will do it.

00:34:12.200 --> 00:34:15.210
And if we're doing it, it'll be more fun to make an impression.

00:34:15.210 --> 00:34:17.280
Don't you agree, guys?

00:34:19.350 --> 00:34:20.240
See?

00:34:21.640 --> 00:34:22.500
Yeah.

00:34:23.690 --> 00:34:25.850
What are you two smiling about?

00:34:25.850 --> 00:34:27.110
Because, you know...

00:34:27.110 --> 00:34:27.940
Right.

00:34:27.940 --> 00:34:30.920
If something interesting happened, you could at least tell me.

00:34:31.480 --> 00:34:32.760
See, it's okay.

00:34:33.130 --> 00:34:34.090
Yeah.

00:34:34.090 --> 00:34:35.450
What?

00:34:35.450 --> 00:34:38.640
We're friends, so don't keep secrets!

00:34:44.930 --> 00:34:46.980
Myao, you're going home?

00:34:46.980 --> 00:34:47.810
Yeah.

00:34:48.530 --> 00:34:52.150
There's no reason for me
to stay here any longer.

00:34:52.830 --> 00:34:55.990
There's no need to protect her either.

00:34:56.760 --> 00:34:59.300
I'm going where I ought to be.

00:34:59.300 --> 00:35:00.370
Thank you...

00:35:01.820 --> 00:35:03.290
for saving me.

00:35:05.440 --> 00:35:06.660
Forget it.

00:35:14.960 --> 00:35:16.030
Oh no!

00:35:16.030 --> 00:35:17.180
The magic will wear off!

00:35:17.830 --> 00:35:18.680
Makino!

00:35:18.680 --> 00:35:19.300
What?

00:35:19.300 --> 00:35:21.930
Like I said, the magic will wear off!

00:35:21.930 --> 00:35:24.390
By magic, do you mean the Monitor?

00:35:23.150 --> 00:35:24.390
Oh, here it is!

00:35:24.980 --> 00:35:27.100
I put magic in your Monitor too, right?

00:35:27.460 --> 00:35:28.290
Yeah.

00:35:28.290 --> 00:35:30.060
That's going to be canceled!

00:35:32.150 --> 00:35:34.280
Like I said...

00:35:34.530 --> 00:35:37.500
We're supposed to be in our homes now!

00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:40.490
If the day changes and they see us here, it'll be suspicious!

00:35:43.830 --> 00:35:45.280
That's late!

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:47.080
We have to get home quickly!

00:35:47.400 --> 00:35:49.120
We'll meet up again tomorrow night.

00:35:50.650 --> 00:35:52.230
Um...

00:35:52.230 --> 00:35:53.170
See you tomorrow!

00:35:55.910 --> 00:35:56.900
Um...

00:35:58.200 --> 00:36:00.730
M-Me too.

00:36:01.660 --> 00:36:02.620
See you again.

00:36:04.630 --> 00:36:07.060
See you again, tomorrow.

00:36:09.470 --> 00:36:10.540
Right!

00:36:10.540 --> 00:36:11.900
S-See you again.

00:36:12.520 --> 00:36:12.940
Um...

00:36:15.130 --> 00:36:16.360
See you again.

00:36:19.580 --> 00:36:20.420
Yes!

00:36:37.870 --> 00:36:39.790
Rocking my heart!

00:36:51.330 --> 00:36:54.350
I'm seriously hooked, my heart is taken.

00:36:54.350 --> 00:36:57.360
How is her plan going?

00:36:57.360 --> 00:36:58.610
Pretend to be frail?

00:36:58.610 --> 00:36:59.990
Or act mature?

00:36:59.990 --> 00:37:01.900
I don't want to let it go to anyone.

00:37:01.900 --> 00:37:03.320
Bubbling carbonated drink.

00:37:03.320 --> 00:37:06.430
She's a complete fake airhead.

00:37:06.430 --> 00:37:09.370
She's letting out a strong pink aura.

00:37:09.370 --> 00:37:10.790
Don't let your guard down.

00:37:10.790 --> 00:37:13.670
All alone, I'll polish myself every night.

00:37:13.670 --> 00:37:15.480
Turn around and face me, darling!

00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:21.590
At times like this, we should try to cooperate with darling.

00:37:21.590 --> 00:37:24.130
Don't mind how others look at you.

00:37:24.130 --> 00:37:25.680
That's right, we won't lose.

00:37:25.680 --> 00:37:27.940
Wink your eyes. Come on, baby.

00:37:27.940 --> 00:37:29.220
Here we go!

00:37:29.220 --> 00:37:30.410
I My Me.

00:37:30.410 --> 00:37:31.770
I am myself.

00:37:31.770 --> 00:37:33.220
You are yourself.

00:37:33.220 --> 00:37:35.230
After making you look back,

00:37:35.690 --> 00:37:39.400
betrayals are okay, but holding grudges isn't.

00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:42.650
Aim for love with a vigilant eye, love.

00:37:46.240 --> 00:37:47.870
What's so funny?

00:37:48.300 --> 00:37:50.530
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:37:50.530 --> 00:37:52.400
Don't laugh, you guys!

00:37:52.400 --> 00:37:54.790
Hey, stop it!

00:38:04.330 --> 00:38:05.770
Oh, you're here.

00:38:10.630 --> 00:38:11.810
I won't forget...

00:38:14.530 --> 00:38:16.910
this sight we all saw together.

00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:19.520
I won't forget.

00:38:22.660 --> 00:38:23.810
Forever.

00:38:45.790 --> 00:38:46.680
Hey.

00:38:47.300 --> 00:38:48.550
What?

00:38:48.890 --> 00:38:51.430
I'm happy you invited me,

00:38:51.430 --> 00:38:53.140
but is it all right?

00:38:53.140 --> 00:38:54.520
I hear this place is expensive.

00:38:55.300 --> 00:38:58.230
Exchanging SVC synthetic sashimi for two months of drinking money...

00:38:58.230 --> 00:39:01.380
doesn't really balance out,

00:39:01.380 --> 00:39:03.900
but I guess it's better for my liver.

00:39:05.670 --> 00:39:06.600
And...

00:39:07.830 --> 00:39:11.990
I wanted to talk with you somewhere that didn't have Image Collection Devices.

00:39:23.370 --> 00:39:24.590
Good evening!

00:39:32.960 --> 00:39:34.190
What's wrong?

00:39:34.830 --> 00:39:37.420
Yabe says she wants to go home.

00:39:37.420 --> 00:39:40.020
I'm opposed to that.

00:39:40.670 --> 00:39:42.730
Yabe-san, you're going home?

00:39:43.010 --> 00:39:44.010
Yeah.

00:39:44.010 --> 00:39:48.250
My fever's down, and it's been a while since then...

00:39:48.250 --> 00:39:49.870
so I thought it'd be all right now.

00:39:49.870 --> 00:39:51.950
There's no way it'd be all right.

00:39:52.440 --> 00:39:54.490
Two thugs attacked you.

00:39:54.490 --> 00:39:57.940
Kawabata died, but there's one more.

00:39:57.940 --> 00:40:00.680
According to the information I stole from the police servers,

00:40:00.680 --> 00:40:02.170
it's someone named Nakamura.

00:40:02.800 --> 00:40:05.320
He might be after you.

00:40:05.320 --> 00:40:07.140
It isn't safe for you to go home now.

00:40:12.380 --> 00:40:13.720
I know that.

00:40:14.280 --> 00:40:15.540
I know that, but...

00:40:17.750 --> 00:40:18.930
Um...

00:40:19.280 --> 00:40:22.400
Why were you attacked?

00:40:23.900 --> 00:40:27.990
Makino, you always ask questions that are rather difficult to ask.

00:40:28.260 --> 00:40:30.320
I-I'm sorry.

00:40:30.320 --> 00:40:32.170
You don't need to apologize.

00:40:34.410 --> 00:40:36.140
DC...

00:40:36.140 --> 00:40:39.540
Do you know what deformed characters are?

00:40:39.900 --> 00:40:42.380
You mean the celluloid videos from the past century, right?

00:40:42.380 --> 00:40:44.250
They were called ani-something.

00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:46.290
Animation.

00:40:46.290 --> 00:40:48.210
Videos that aren't real.

00:40:49.240 --> 00:40:52.900
I love those DCs.

00:40:52.900 --> 00:40:54.260
Do you think I'm strange?

00:40:55.010 --> 00:40:56.170
Why?

00:40:56.170 --> 00:40:57.560
Not at all.

00:40:57.960 --> 00:40:59.520
It's not strange at all!

00:41:01.360 --> 00:41:02.840
Thank you.

00:41:02.840 --> 00:41:06.620
And so, I still love DCs.

00:41:07.300 --> 00:41:11.110
I wanted to be a designer and drew many things.

00:41:11.770 --> 00:41:13.120
Let me see.

00:41:13.120 --> 00:41:14.070
What?

00:41:24.750 --> 00:41:27.860
Yabe-san drew this?

00:41:27.860 --> 00:41:28.840
Yeah.

00:41:29.460 --> 00:41:32.890
It's manga art from an Internet community.

00:41:34.160 --> 00:41:36.260
So it's a deformed character.

00:41:36.260 --> 00:41:37.390
Right.

00:41:37.390 --> 00:41:41.890
Yabe Yuko's ID was found on a site that accepts this stuff.

00:41:41.890 --> 00:41:45.280
I knew she loved drawing pictures,

00:41:45.280 --> 00:41:49.300
but I didn't know she participated in that.

00:41:49.300 --> 00:41:51.320
Go back one level, please.

00:41:54.110 --> 00:41:55.800
There are six pictures there, right?

00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:56.450
Yeah.

00:41:57.710 --> 00:42:01.290
The deceased victims drew them.

00:42:03.150 --> 00:42:06.750
It's still unconfirmed because HQ hasn't completed its research yet,

00:42:07.630 --> 00:42:11.610
but all six victims contributed to that site.

00:42:13.240 --> 00:42:15.250
Weren't there seven victims?

00:42:16.140 --> 00:42:20.340
The Prefecture Police don't consider Kawabata a victim in the killings.

00:42:22.070 --> 00:42:26.700
The Police discovered that the victims have to be girls.

00:42:28.860 --> 00:42:30.620
Kawabata Ryu is a male.

00:42:30.620 --> 00:42:33.030
Thus, he was not supposed to be a target.

00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:36.270
Display list 78.

00:42:39.090 --> 00:42:40.250
What's this picture?

00:42:43.020 --> 00:42:45.250
Kawabata drew it?

00:42:46.300 --> 00:42:48.960
I had him draw this when we met in the real world.

00:42:49.210 --> 00:42:51.150
You met him in the real world?

00:42:51.150 --> 00:42:52.920
Even though he attacked you?

00:42:53.210 --> 00:42:54.500
Yes.

00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:58.650
Some people praised the pictures I uploaded to the Internet.

00:42:58.650 --> 00:43:01.020
And Kawabata was one of them?

00:43:01.020 --> 00:43:03.290
He was gentle at first.

00:43:03.290 --> 00:43:06.250
We had a nice talk about DCs we liked.

00:43:07.910 --> 00:43:09.100
Then...

00:43:09.940 --> 00:43:11.570
How can you call that original?!

00:43:11.570 --> 00:43:13.150
What are you doing?!

00:43:13.400 --> 00:43:16.100
You're copying the design of that art piece!

00:43:16.100 --> 00:43:17.320
I'm not!

00:43:17.320 --> 00:43:18.990
This is an original!

00:43:19.750 --> 00:43:25.550
Your pictures profane the art piece we respect so much!

00:43:25.550 --> 00:43:26.670
What are you saying?!

00:43:26.670 --> 00:43:27.360
I'm not—

00:43:27.360 --> 00:43:28.040
Shut up!

00:43:32.130 --> 00:43:34.600
Because of people like you,

00:43:34.600 --> 00:43:37.840
the world denies the greatness of that piece.

00:43:38.950 --> 00:43:39.720
So...

00:43:41.620 --> 00:43:43.100
die.

00:43:44.290 --> 00:43:45.950
But he died instead.

00:43:47.400 --> 00:43:48.660
If we thought about it logically,

00:43:48.660 --> 00:43:53.110
we'd conclude that something went wrong, and Nakamura killed Kawabata.

00:43:54.080 --> 00:43:55.690
Something is strange, though.

00:43:56.850 --> 00:43:58.070
What is it?

00:43:59.210 --> 00:44:01.780
All six victims who were killed...

00:44:02.250 --> 00:44:04.120
were missing something.

00:44:05.480 --> 00:44:06.450
Their internal organs?

00:44:07.970 --> 00:44:08.930
Right.

00:44:09.830 --> 00:44:11.650
Their internal organs were missing.

00:44:13.130 --> 00:44:18.190
When Aikawa was found dead this morning, hers had been extracted too.

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:20.930
How scary...

00:44:21.270 --> 00:44:24.410
It's not normal to remove internal organs, is it?

00:44:24.410 --> 00:44:26.890
Someone like that could be the attacker.

00:44:26.890 --> 00:44:28.760
It's not safe for you to go home.

00:44:30.120 --> 00:44:33.510
But I want to change my clothes.

00:44:33.510 --> 00:44:36.160
I want to see my father and mother too.

00:44:37.830 --> 00:44:40.690
Is your home in Area A?

00:44:40.690 --> 00:44:41.890
Yes.

00:44:41.890 --> 00:44:44.940
If you live in Area A, then Area Security should be on patrol.

00:44:44.940 --> 00:44:46.900
You should be safe.

00:44:46.900 --> 00:44:50.040
It would be a problem if they saw us taking her home.

00:44:50.660 --> 00:44:55.960
And we'd have to explain why Yabe was staying here, and about Myao too.

00:44:56.500 --> 00:44:57.660
I see.

00:44:58.980 --> 00:45:01.760
It would be nice if you could delete memories with magic too.

00:45:02.430 --> 00:45:05.810
If your memories were erased,
you wouldn't even be able to go home.

00:45:05.810 --> 00:45:07.570
You're right.

00:45:07.570 --> 00:45:10.300
You wouldn't be able to call the police either, would you?

00:45:11.990 --> 00:45:12.880
You're right.

00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:13.310
What?

00:45:14.060 --> 00:45:15.470
We can use magic!

00:45:31.240 --> 00:45:32.000
Okay.

00:45:32.770 --> 00:45:35.310
First, we send Makino home with our usual magic.

00:45:35.960 --> 00:45:38.910
I'll give you a signal when it's 24:00.

00:45:38.910 --> 00:45:42.680
Yabe, you pretend to have amnesia and wander onto Makino's property.

00:45:43.330 --> 00:45:45.760
Then, hit the door hard.

00:45:54.440 --> 00:45:56.980
Makino, when you see Yabe,

00:45:56.980 --> 00:46:00.160
push the security call button on your home Monitor.

00:46:00.160 --> 00:46:03.030
Then the Area Security people will come.

00:46:03.030 --> 00:46:08.450
After they take Yabe into custody, we can leave the rest to the adults, and the plan is complete.

00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:13.620
Also, since we've become good friends, we'll stop referring to each other like strangers.

00:46:13.620 --> 00:46:14.620
Hazuki.

00:46:15.100 --> 00:46:15.580
Ayumi.

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:16.540
Yuko.

00:46:17.330 --> 00:46:19.030
And me.

00:46:19.030 --> 00:46:21.130
I'll include Myao too.

00:46:21.130 --> 00:46:22.510
She gets lonely.

00:46:22.510 --> 00:46:24.010
Really?

00:46:24.010 --> 00:46:26.350
So I put a tracer on her.

00:46:26.350 --> 00:46:28.110
Wh-Where?

00:46:29.960 --> 00:46:32.110
Well then, see you later.

00:46:32.110 --> 00:46:33.070
Later.

00:46:34.470 --> 00:46:35.290
Me too.

00:46:35.290 --> 00:46:35.890
See you.

00:46:36.830 --> 00:46:37.810
Hazuki!

00:46:39.210 --> 00:46:41.540
I might not be able to come for a while,

00:46:41.540 --> 00:46:43.860
but teach me the moves for next time, okay?

00:46:45.290 --> 00:46:47.510
Y-You're okay with someone like me?

00:46:47.510 --> 00:46:47.820
Yabe-sa—

00:46:47.820 --> 00:46:49.470
Yuko.

00:46:49.470 --> 00:46:50.390
Right?

00:46:51.360 --> 00:46:52.660
Hazuki.

00:46:56.370 --> 00:46:57.250
Yeah!

00:47:14.040 --> 00:47:17.150
This is the D&S Security Center.

00:47:17.150 --> 00:47:20.730
Um, there's a stranger at the door.

00:47:22.030 --> 00:47:24.260
We have confirmed your Monitor address.

00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:26.300
This is Makino Hazuki-san's residence, correct?

00:47:27.240 --> 00:47:27.950
Yes.

00:47:28.450 --> 00:47:30.560
We will send our Area staff immediately.

00:47:31.420 --> 00:47:32.760
Please do.

00:47:35.520 --> 00:47:37.650
Just a little longer, Yuko.

00:47:42.420 --> 00:47:46.800
We'll take custody of the person you reported.

00:47:46.800 --> 00:47:50.590
We'll file a report to the police too.

00:47:50.590 --> 00:47:51.950
Thank you.

00:47:55.570 --> 00:47:56.470
Down?

00:48:14.010 --> 00:48:15.700
Yuko...

00:48:15.700 --> 00:48:22.080
Sign: See you again

00:48:17.560 --> 00:48:18.680
See you again.

00:48:25.630 --> 00:48:27.690
Three days have passed since then.

00:48:30.510 --> 00:48:34.190
It was a normal morning for me.

00:48:35.160 --> 00:48:36.430
The only thing different was...

00:48:36.960 --> 00:48:40.670
that we'd promised to see each other again.

00:48:40.670 --> 00:48:45.290
So for three days, I'd been waiting for Yuko,

00:48:45.290 --> 00:48:47.740
who'd been taken into custody by Area Security, to send an email back.

00:48:46.400 --> 00:48:51.450
Sign: See you again

00:48:48.640 --> 00:48:50.730
How's Yuko doing?

00:48:52.940 --> 00:48:53.790
An email?

00:48:54.770 --> 00:48:56.830
Could it be...

00:49:00.090 --> 00:49:01.100
No way.

00:49:06.120 --> 00:49:07.150
Why?

00:49:28.230 --> 00:49:29.960
Yuko's dead.

00:49:31.160 --> 00:49:33.530
She's no longer with us.

00:49:39.320 --> 00:49:40.750
Myao is the killer?!

00:49:40.750 --> 00:49:42.630
She killed Nakamura and Yuko?!

00:49:43.040 --> 00:49:44.390
Their livers were removed?!

00:49:44.850 --> 00:49:45.880
What is this?!

00:49:48.570 --> 00:49:50.420
Did someone fail?

00:49:50.420 --> 00:49:53.970
I called Area Security.

00:49:53.970 --> 00:49:57.230
I saw them take Yuko into protective custody.

00:49:58.260 --> 00:50:00.140
Who killed Yuko and where?

00:50:01.070 --> 00:50:04.830
Look, the videos are still on my Monitor.

00:50:06.050 --> 00:50:09.190
This is Area Security G02254.

00:50:09.190 --> 00:50:12.930
We have taken a person into custody at Area 122: Makino's house.

00:50:12.930 --> 00:50:13.900
Center, confirmed.

00:50:13.900 --> 00:50:16.570
And this is what the police have.

00:50:16.570 --> 00:50:19.960
This is Area Security G02253.

00:50:19.960 --> 00:50:23.910
We have taken a person into custody at Area 122: Makino's house.

00:50:23.910 --> 00:50:25.540
Center, confirmed.

00:50:26.020 --> 00:50:30.940
And the person taken into custody isn't Yuko, but some woman I've never seen.

00:50:30.940 --> 00:50:33.260
How could that be?

00:50:35.570 --> 00:50:36.510
Magic...

00:50:38.100 --> 00:50:38.850
Huh?

00:50:39.250 --> 00:50:41.680
Someone must've used it.

00:50:42.080 --> 00:50:44.270
A magic stronger than ours.

00:50:44.940 --> 00:50:48.110
Hazuki, what are you saying?

00:50:48.860 --> 00:50:50.440
I'm the magician!

00:50:50.980 --> 00:50:52.570
I'm the <i>only</i> magician!

00:50:52.900 --> 00:50:54.400
We lose.

00:50:56.090 --> 00:50:59.120
Yabe is dead, and all her information is lost.

00:51:00.310 --> 00:51:05.970
We can't prove the information here is real, so they'll treat it as fake.

00:51:05.970 --> 00:51:09.690
However, the fact that Yabe was killed is real.

00:51:17.840 --> 00:51:18.680
Get out!

00:51:19.060 --> 00:51:20.960
Everyone, get out!

00:51:24.160 --> 00:51:26.640
Mio was upset.

00:51:27.160 --> 00:51:29.750
The program she's so proud of was beaten,

00:51:29.750 --> 00:51:31.680
in a way she never expected.

00:51:32.730 --> 00:51:33.900
That's true.

00:51:37.010 --> 00:51:39.570
Why do they kill?

00:51:42.870 --> 00:51:44.710
The reason doesn't matter.

00:51:44.710 --> 00:51:46.540
Those who can kill will kill.

00:51:48.450 --> 00:51:50.420
There are more killers.

00:51:51.860 --> 00:51:53.090
The smell of beasts emanates...

00:51:54.390 --> 00:51:56.270
from people like them.

00:51:57.900 --> 00:52:00.170
The smell of beasts?

00:52:01.880 --> 00:52:03.740
Makino, you should go home.

00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:07.700
Your monitored cage should be safe.

00:52:09.470 --> 00:52:10.330
Ko—

00:52:21.670 --> 00:52:23.200
I just sent in the list.

00:52:24.390 --> 00:52:25.270
Thank you.

00:52:25.270 --> 00:52:26.380
You've been a great help.

00:52:27.680 --> 00:52:31.630
I'll do some research to see if there are any other related articles.

00:52:32.020 --> 00:52:33.310
Yeah.

00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:35.710
Don't get too involved in this.

00:52:36.020 --> 00:52:38.040
Are you worried about me?

00:52:38.040 --> 00:52:40.970
Your mother was like that too.

00:52:40.970 --> 00:52:42.540
I'm fine.

00:52:42.540 --> 00:52:44.550
I'm different from my mother.

00:52:44.550 --> 00:52:46.100
I believe in you.

00:52:46.750 --> 00:52:48.910
So then, I'll see you later.

00:52:48.910 --> 00:52:49.640
Yeah.

00:52:49.640 --> 00:52:50.560
Bye.

00:52:52.580 --> 00:52:55.280
He sure is a worrywart.

00:52:59.120 --> 00:53:00.000
Who?

00:52:59.300 --> 00:53:00.820
Don't look back.

00:53:01.930 --> 00:53:04.280
Continue to listen.

00:53:04.280 --> 00:53:05.580
Kono-san.

00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:10.160
It's dangerous for students to be walking around at this time.

00:53:11.450 --> 00:53:14.920
Tsuzuki and Makino might be killed next.

00:53:15.530 --> 00:53:18.170
If it's that important, you can report to the police—

00:53:18.170 --> 00:53:21.090
The killer can see any information given to the police.

00:53:23.630 --> 00:53:28.500
The information on the Internet gets rewritten for the killer's benefit.

00:53:28.500 --> 00:53:32.730
Luckily, the Image Collection Devices can't record sound.

00:53:33.590 --> 00:53:37.410
So the killer doesn't know that I'm here,

00:53:37.410 --> 00:53:40.360
and that I know the truth which he thought had been deleted.

00:53:40.700 --> 00:53:43.820
What do you know?

00:53:44.710 --> 00:53:51.160
Before Yabe Yuko was killed, D&S Area Security took her into custody at Makino Hazuki's house.

00:53:52.450 --> 00:53:56.040
I never heard that from the police.

00:53:57.320 --> 00:54:03.470
And if you overwrote the action log, D&S and the police would know quickly—

00:54:04.780 --> 00:54:06.670
D&S and the police?

00:54:07.880 --> 00:54:11.350
Ishida is the great-grandchild of the SVC's founder.

00:54:11.920 --> 00:54:13.960
I am Ishida Riichiro.

00:54:14.840 --> 00:54:16.170
No way.

00:54:16.170 --> 00:54:17.260
Ishida did it?

00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.410
There's no time to confirm that.

00:54:21.490 --> 00:54:24.610
I entrust Makino and Tsuzuki to you.

00:54:28.170 --> 00:54:29.360
Wait!

00:54:33.460 --> 00:54:35.080
Kono-san?

00:54:38.040 --> 00:54:46.470
Sign: Safety First

00:54:45.260 --> 00:54:46.470
Mio...

00:54:46.920 --> 00:54:50.060
Hurry up and escape!

00:54:50.470 --> 00:54:51.680
I'll definitely find it!

00:54:52.580 --> 00:54:54.600
I'm the only magician!

00:54:55.360 --> 00:54:57.940
Whether it's broken into bits or just hidden...

00:54:59.700 --> 00:55:00.900
What is this?

00:55:01.450 --> 00:55:03.580
Why are people like them...

00:55:08.320 --> 00:55:11.040
W-Wait a second!

00:55:22.660 --> 00:55:27.800
At this moment, the Prefecture Police are investigating the explosion at C-421-2.

00:55:28.750 --> 00:55:31.280
The roads are being sealed off,

00:55:29.080 --> 00:55:29.760
Mio...

00:55:31.280 --> 00:55:33.570
so please follow the directions from your Navigation.

00:55:34.810 --> 00:55:37.150
SVC's synthetic foods

00:55:37.150 --> 00:55:41.060
are made from the world's first synthesized proteins aiding healthy growth—

00:55:37.890 --> 00:55:39.330
It won't work.

00:55:39.330 --> 00:55:41.050
I can't connect to her.

00:55:47.840 --> 00:55:48.780
No way...

00:55:48.780 --> 00:55:49.750
Mio too?

00:55:52.750 --> 00:55:53.450
Who is it?

00:55:56.750 --> 00:55:59.420
I'm from D&S Area Service.

00:56:00.130 --> 00:56:03.730
Your father has ordered a security option.

00:56:03.730 --> 00:56:05.000
My father?

00:56:05.390 --> 00:56:06.340
Yes.

00:56:06.340 --> 00:56:08.500
He seems very worried.

00:56:08.500 --> 00:56:08.970
I see.

00:56:10.070 --> 00:56:14.270
We need to send confirmation that we've successfully made Real Contact.

00:56:14.270 --> 00:56:17.030
Let us access your inside Monitor, please.

00:56:26.790 --> 00:56:27.850
This is the one, right?

00:56:27.850 --> 00:56:29.200
Oh, yes.

00:56:29.720 --> 00:56:34.080
So you administer the locks for the whole house using this, right?

00:56:34.080 --> 00:56:34.890
Yes.

00:56:34.890 --> 00:56:37.090
And this...

00:56:43.760 --> 00:56:44.700
The locks?

00:56:48.940 --> 00:56:50.130
It's been dangerous lately...

00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:54.030
so I locked down the whole house.

00:57:06.710 --> 00:57:07.570
The lock...

00:57:08.360 --> 00:57:10.900
You have to lock your doors properly.

00:57:12.900 --> 00:57:15.170
This is a specially manufactured taser.

00:57:15.170 --> 00:57:16.700
Once it shocks the core of your body,

00:57:17.200 --> 00:57:19.430
you won't even notice that you're dead.

00:57:20.340 --> 00:57:21.370
The home locks...

00:57:21.740 --> 00:57:22.600
The locks...

00:57:22.600 --> 00:57:23.590
Where?

00:57:24.250 --> 00:57:24.960
An email?

00:58:01.900 --> 00:58:05.660
How dare you take out Alvil.

00:58:08.650 --> 00:58:11.170
I'll make you suffer the same fate as Yabe—

00:58:18.570 --> 00:58:19.930
Rei Myao-san...

00:58:21.070 --> 00:58:22.050
Can you move?

00:58:22.050 --> 00:58:23.160
Yes.

00:58:23.160 --> 00:58:24.900
Escape from this city, now!

00:58:24.900 --> 00:58:26.100
What?

00:58:43.500 --> 00:58:46.330
A stray cat is trying to get in my way?

00:58:46.330 --> 00:58:49.040
I won't let you do as you wish!

00:58:49.750 --> 00:58:51.290
Run, Hazuki!

00:58:51.670 --> 00:58:52.880
Rei Myao-san, what about you?!

00:58:52.880 --> 00:58:55.720
I'll stop them!

00:59:05.560 --> 00:59:07.370
Hazuki, survive!

00:59:07.370 --> 00:59:09.190
For Yuko too!

00:59:11.820 --> 00:59:13.320
Yuko...

00:59:15.650 --> 00:59:17.070
Sign: See you again

00:59:26.820 --> 00:59:28.570
Run, Hazuki!

00:59:57.530 --> 00:59:59.360
Sorry to call you here so late.

01:00:00.100 --> 01:00:01.730
It's okay.

01:00:01.730 --> 01:00:03.990
But why here?

01:00:04.420 --> 01:00:06.680
You could have chosen the Center too.

01:00:06.680 --> 01:00:07.930
About that...

01:00:08.560 --> 01:00:10.880
It'll be hard to leave a record here.

01:00:12.550 --> 01:00:13.840
What happened?

01:00:14.230 --> 01:00:21.430
I want you to protect Makino Hazuki-san and Tsuzuki Mio-san, whom I'm in charge of.

01:00:21.850 --> 01:00:25.390
Why are you asking me and not the police?

01:00:26.160 --> 01:00:31.850
When Yabe-san was killed, someone apparently rewrote the police data.

01:00:32.490 --> 01:00:35.880
That's pretty disturbing.

01:00:35.880 --> 01:00:37.820
Who would do that?

01:00:38.690 --> 01:00:41.480
It must be Administrative Officer Ishida.

01:00:41.480 --> 01:00:43.230
That's bad.

01:01:12.310 --> 01:01:14.650
You woke up?

01:01:16.070 --> 01:01:18.410
Yabe and Tsuzuki were taken down.

01:01:18.410 --> 01:01:21.610
I thought they got you too.

01:01:22.560 --> 01:01:23.840
Are you injured?

01:01:23.840 --> 01:01:24.570
No.

01:01:24.940 --> 01:01:26.240
Want something to eat?

01:01:26.950 --> 01:01:28.540
Though I only have synthesized food.

01:01:29.450 --> 01:01:31.310
I assume this place isn't safe anymore.

01:01:32.050 --> 01:01:33.800
Makino, you should leave here quickly—

01:01:35.340 --> 01:01:36.240
Makino?

01:01:37.020 --> 01:01:38.040
I don't...

01:01:38.850 --> 01:01:40.470
I don't want to be alone anymore.

01:01:41.530 --> 01:01:43.730
I was able to meet people.

01:01:43.730 --> 01:01:45.930
I was able to meet people I could believe in.

01:01:47.230 --> 01:01:50.020
What can I do all alone?

01:01:53.740 --> 01:01:55.130
Do you want to come with me?

01:01:56.720 --> 01:01:57.780
Where?

01:01:58.830 --> 01:01:59.860
The SVC.

01:02:00.580 --> 01:02:02.850
That's where it all began.

01:02:15.910 --> 01:02:17.710
You threw away your Monitor?

01:02:18.340 --> 01:02:23.170
We're bound by the Monitor in every part of our life...

01:02:23.810 --> 01:02:25.510
as long as we're in this city.

01:03:53.800 --> 01:03:55.680
Just a little...

01:03:56.290 --> 01:03:59.080
A short break, please.

01:04:02.960 --> 01:04:07.060
How far do we need to walk?

01:04:07.060 --> 01:04:10.220
It's about fifteen kilometers until we reach the SVC.

01:04:10.220 --> 01:04:11.530
Fifteen kilometers?

01:04:12.140 --> 01:04:14.180
You can go at your own pace.

01:04:14.180 --> 01:04:15.480
Just keep walking.

01:04:24.280 --> 01:04:26.940
We can only escape.

01:04:28.060 --> 01:04:30.770
Because we're running away from the System of Society,

01:04:30.770 --> 01:04:33.790
we need to seize our future with our own hands.

01:04:33.790 --> 01:04:37.000
Otherwise, we won't even be able to feel the heat of the sun.

01:04:40.860 --> 01:04:41.980
Let's survive.

01:04:46.160 --> 01:04:47.530
For those who didn't.

01:05:16.050 --> 01:05:16.930
Where am I?

01:05:17.600 --> 01:05:18.770
Kunugi-san?

01:05:19.470 --> 01:05:23.400
Unfortunately, Detective Kunugi is at work.

01:05:24.700 --> 01:05:27.770
Welcome to the SVC center.

01:05:27.770 --> 01:05:29.110
SVC?

01:05:30.070 --> 01:05:36.200
Counselor of Community Center 122, Fuwa Shizue-san.

01:05:36.470 --> 01:05:38.020
Administrative Officer Ishida!

01:05:38.980 --> 01:05:42.160
You killed my students?

01:05:42.160 --> 01:05:45.450
I wouldn't do such a thing.

01:05:45.450 --> 01:05:46.680
You're lying!

01:05:46.680 --> 01:05:49.630
Quit watching me from a Monitor and show yourself!

01:05:49.630 --> 01:05:52.230
There's no need for that.

01:05:52.230 --> 01:05:55.010
You're right next to me.

01:05:55.670 --> 01:05:57.200
What do you mean?

01:05:58.340 --> 01:05:59.430
Oh, excuse me.

01:05:59.430 --> 01:06:01.180
It seems I have visitors.

01:06:01.870 --> 01:06:04.780
Oh my, oh my.

01:06:04.780 --> 01:06:08.330
They've come all the way for me.

01:06:08.330 --> 01:06:10.650
Makino-san... Kono-san...

01:06:11.710 --> 01:06:12.860
Why?

01:06:13.750 --> 01:06:16.570
I'll send something to welcome them.

01:06:17.180 --> 01:06:20.540
Escape, Kono-san, Makino-san!

01:06:21.100 --> 01:06:22.780
Sorry.

01:06:22.780 --> 01:06:25.000
It's because I used the main entrance.

01:06:25.530 --> 01:06:27.160
They would've found us sooner or later.

01:06:27.160 --> 01:06:27.960
Don't worry.

01:06:28.610 --> 01:06:29.870
Makino, let's run!

01:06:46.950 --> 01:06:47.910
This way.

01:07:01.710 --> 01:07:03.450
It's all my fault.

01:07:03.860 --> 01:07:06.670
It's my fault for taking you with me.

01:07:15.350 --> 01:07:16.510
Listen closely, Makino.

01:07:17.050 --> 01:07:19.750
I'll distract the security robots.

01:07:19.750 --> 01:07:23.270
While I do that, you escape.

01:07:23.270 --> 01:07:24.960
What about you, Kono-san?

01:07:24.960 --> 01:07:26.570
I'll be fine.

01:07:27.310 --> 01:07:29.440
So don't give up.

01:07:31.770 --> 01:07:32.780
That's right.

01:07:32.780 --> 01:07:33.360
Don't give up!

01:07:33.960 --> 01:07:36.410
You're going to survive, right?

01:07:39.020 --> 01:07:41.200
For Yuko and Mio too!

01:07:41.580 --> 01:07:43.110
Rei Myao-san!

01:07:43.110 --> 01:07:44.750
So you're alive.

01:07:44.750 --> 01:07:47.420
Just barely, I guess.

01:07:48.070 --> 01:07:52.940
But my presence here won't really change the situation...

01:07:52.940 --> 01:07:54.050
I agree.

01:07:54.770 --> 01:07:55.630
But...

01:07:55.630 --> 01:07:58.720
we're alive.

01:07:59.300 --> 01:08:02.680
I feel Ayumi's warmth.

01:08:05.230 --> 01:08:05.980
They're coming!

01:08:34.020 --> 01:08:35.280
They stopped?

01:08:36.000 --> 01:08:38.260
Sorry about that.

01:08:39.370 --> 01:08:42.220
The security system was
undergoing maintenance.

01:08:43.090 --> 01:08:46.180
Apparently the security robots were in auto-target mode.

01:08:49.610 --> 01:08:52.150
Are any of you hurt?

01:08:53.660 --> 01:08:55.110
Kunugi-san?

01:08:55.110 --> 01:09:00.010
Detective Kunugi seems to have succeeded in protecting the lost children.

01:09:00.010 --> 01:09:01.900
That was close.

01:09:02.440 --> 01:09:03.450
Close?

01:09:04.050 --> 01:09:06.310
Didn't you cause that?

01:09:06.310 --> 01:09:09.560
Come to think of it, she said something like that too.

01:09:10.460 --> 01:09:11.420
She?

01:09:11.660 --> 01:09:18.380
The woman who committed suicide with the suspected serial killer four years ago.

01:09:18.380 --> 01:09:21.720
16-year-old serial killer

01:09:18.720 --> 01:09:20.850
Fuwa Yukie-san.

01:09:20.850 --> 01:09:21.720
Oh, that's right.

01:09:22.100 --> 01:09:26.430
Detective Kunugi brought her here that time as well.

01:09:27.220 --> 01:09:33.370
Like you, she was trying to find out the truth behind the serial murders.

01:09:43.370 --> 01:09:47.030
So, you're innocent, Rei Myao-san?

01:09:47.510 --> 01:09:50.500
Leave it to me, and I'll make sure everything turns out okay.

01:09:51.180 --> 01:09:52.570
Good to know.

01:09:55.010 --> 01:09:57.210
Why are you here, Detective?

01:09:58.310 --> 01:10:00.820
Fuwa-san asked me to come.

01:10:00.820 --> 01:10:04.720
She said that you know the truth behind the murders, and that you're in danger.

01:10:05.010 --> 01:10:06.700
Really?

01:10:06.700 --> 01:10:09.720
So is Ishida the real culprit, after all?

01:10:10.140 --> 01:10:12.470
There's no proof.

01:10:12.470 --> 01:10:14.970
But first, we have to deal with you guys.

01:10:15.650 --> 01:10:18.440
Thank you for that.

01:10:18.840 --> 01:10:22.400
It's an adult's job to guide children.

01:10:24.210 --> 01:10:26.010
It's this floor.

01:10:27.850 --> 01:10:29.660
What's here?

01:10:29.660 --> 01:10:31.790
The truth behind the murders.

01:10:31.790 --> 01:10:33.260
Now get off already.

01:10:34.070 --> 01:10:35.080
You too.

01:10:36.740 --> 01:10:38.000
Sorry.

01:10:38.800 --> 01:10:40.640
The sunset was beautiful.

01:10:41.200 --> 01:10:43.800
Detective, what time is it now?

01:10:45.230 --> 01:10:47.670
Oh, right.

01:10:47.670 --> 01:10:48.810
Let's see...

01:10:48.810 --> 01:10:50.360
It's now...

01:10:50.360 --> 01:10:51.770
Almost...

01:10:57.630 --> 01:10:59.060
What's wrong?

01:11:04.410 --> 01:11:05.670
What happened?

01:11:06.460 --> 01:11:07.950
This person was an enemy.

01:11:08.780 --> 01:11:09.830
An enemy?

01:11:10.450 --> 01:11:15.090
We're the only children without Monitors.

01:11:15.090 --> 01:11:19.790
If we asked for the time, an adult would normally reply, "What happened to your Monitor?"

01:11:20.530 --> 01:11:22.690
But he didn't.

01:11:22.690 --> 01:11:25.930
He tried to tell me the time without asking that.

01:11:27.130 --> 01:11:32.050
That's because he already knew we didn't have Monitors.

01:11:32.050 --> 01:11:33.720
So you really are...

01:11:35.520 --> 01:11:37.460
I'm the killer, so...

01:11:39.090 --> 01:11:44.060
If they'd never met me, those two wouldn't have died.

01:11:48.240 --> 01:11:49.660
Don't tell anyone!

01:11:49.660 --> 01:11:51.320
Forget what you just saw.

01:11:51.320 --> 01:11:52.840
Fine.

01:11:52.840 --> 01:11:55.040
I hate troublesome affairs.

01:11:58.310 --> 01:12:03.170
If he hadn't done anything,
I would've gone straight home.

01:12:04.540 --> 01:12:07.050
Instead, he ran away.

01:12:07.050 --> 01:12:10.500
He must not have expected me to fight back.

01:12:15.590 --> 01:12:16.760
Don't look!

01:12:16.760 --> 01:12:18.520
Don't look at me!

01:12:19.120 --> 01:12:25.260
After saying that, Kawabata took a steel pipe and attacked me, just like Nakamura.

01:12:26.190 --> 01:12:28.790
So you killed him?

01:12:28.790 --> 01:12:31.030
You could've escaped!

01:12:32.100 --> 01:12:33.180
I don't know.

01:12:33.850 --> 01:12:34.990
But by the time I realized that,

01:12:38.230 --> 01:12:39.920
Kawabata was already dead.

01:12:41.830 --> 01:12:43.450
I killed him.

01:12:44.130 --> 01:12:45.920
I killed Kawabata.

01:12:45.920 --> 01:12:46.880
And also Nakamura.

01:12:52.410 --> 01:12:55.350
Because I am Loups=Garous,

01:12:56.310 --> 01:12:59.370
a beast hiding in human skin.

01:13:01.040 --> 01:13:06.070
There was a sunflower field near the place where I used to live.

01:13:06.070 --> 01:13:08.260
It was my favorite place.

01:13:08.260 --> 01:13:11.330
I often walked there after leaving my house.

01:13:11.330 --> 01:13:12.860
People didn't go there,

01:13:12.860 --> 01:13:16.610
and I felt like I had the night all to myself.

01:13:16.610 --> 01:13:19.410
That night had a full moon.

01:13:23.790 --> 01:13:27.080
An unknown man suddenly attacked me.

01:13:50.200 --> 01:13:53.700
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

01:13:55.100 --> 01:13:57.660
He kept apologizing.

01:13:58.480 --> 01:14:01.940
He talked about how in the past, he had killed a girl,

01:14:01.940 --> 01:14:05.100
how he'd been caught and sent to a hospital,

01:14:05.100 --> 01:14:11.380
and how his urge to attack girls occasionally flared up, and he couldn't control himself.

01:14:11.380 --> 01:14:13.630
He kept telling me this while he apologized.

01:14:14.850 --> 01:14:18.470
By carrying a knife around,

01:14:18.470 --> 01:14:22.870
he was making his wishes come true — wishes that should never have been granted.

01:14:22.870 --> 01:14:24.420
However, he could never be satisfied.

01:14:24.420 --> 01:14:25.560
He told me that.

01:14:28.710 --> 01:14:31.530
He presented the knife to me, and I took it in my hand.

01:14:38.670 --> 01:14:42.660
And when I saw the nape of his neck...

01:14:50.020 --> 01:14:50.800
Myao.

01:14:52.610 --> 01:14:54.680
I leave Makino to you.

01:15:23.750 --> 01:15:24.860
What?

01:15:24.860 --> 01:15:25.460
It's coming!

01:15:35.330 --> 01:15:36.210
Wha—

01:15:40.790 --> 01:15:42.470
Yo, you're alive?

01:15:43.240 --> 01:15:44.780
Mio!

01:15:44.780 --> 01:15:46.160
Sorry to make you wait.

01:15:47.330 --> 01:15:48.860
Open up!

01:15:50.940 --> 01:15:53.190
Someone open this door!

01:15:53.610 --> 01:15:55.440
Isn't there anyone here?

01:15:55.440 --> 01:15:58.530
You really don't understand, do you?

01:15:59.050 --> 01:16:01.880
Detective Kunugi is dead.

01:16:02.240 --> 01:16:06.580
He won't come back to life, even if you run to his side.

01:16:07.100 --> 01:16:12.500
If you fight and then kill an unregistered girl in order to protect your students,

01:16:12.500 --> 01:16:18.510
my original scenario, in which Detective Kunugi cleared up the situation, will no longer work.

01:16:18.510 --> 01:16:20.860
Many people have died!

01:16:20.860 --> 01:16:22.130
What kind of scenario is that?!

01:16:22.130 --> 01:16:23.560
Do you have any morals?!

01:16:23.560 --> 01:16:25.560
Are you still human?!

01:16:26.220 --> 01:16:34.270
Everything in this world exists to realize the noble ideals of the founder, Suzuki Keitarou.

01:16:34.530 --> 01:16:39.880
I don't know what ideals you're talking about, but there's no way people should die!

01:16:39.880 --> 01:16:41.530
Do you really believe that?

01:16:42.760 --> 01:16:46.680
Suzuki Keitarou survived the war in the previous century.

01:16:46.680 --> 01:16:52.460
With his tragic experiences as a
foundation, he established the SVC.

01:16:52.760 --> 01:16:56.420
He succeeded in developing safe, artificial meat,

01:16:56.420 --> 01:17:01.900
that strongly resembles the real thing, using sunflowers as ingredients.

01:17:02.380 --> 01:17:06.350
As a result, the food shortage around the world has been alleviated,

01:17:06.350 --> 01:17:10.530
and the SVC has become the de facto leader of this country.

01:17:10.530 --> 01:17:15.980
Suzuki Keitarou's ideals were always at the core of the SVC.

01:17:16.300 --> 01:17:20.100
Realization of those ideals requires a society with safe government

01:17:20.100 --> 01:17:23.780
and healthy children, who are entrusted with the future.

01:17:23.780 --> 01:17:26.450
Then why are you killing children?

01:17:26.710 --> 01:17:30.170
You're the one stealing the future from them!

01:17:30.170 --> 01:17:32.370
I'm not letting them go to waste.

01:17:34.350 --> 01:17:39.380
I haven't wasted even a single bit of the children's bodies.

01:17:39.790 --> 01:17:42.790
We're putting them to use for the future.

01:17:44.470 --> 01:17:45.960
Putting them to use?

01:17:47.380 --> 01:17:49.850
I've brought the materials.

01:17:58.150 --> 01:17:59.280
Ouch.

01:18:05.570 --> 01:18:06.620
Where is this?

01:18:07.580 --> 01:18:08.960
Who are these children?

01:18:08.960 --> 01:18:12.950
Alvil, are these the new materials?

01:18:12.950 --> 01:18:14.000
Yes.

01:18:14.000 --> 01:18:17.960
They've been carefully chosen from the Area 122 list.

01:18:18.630 --> 01:18:19.790
List?

01:18:23.100 --> 01:18:27.260
No way, that list of students...

01:18:27.800 --> 01:18:32.730
Thank you for your cooperation, Counselor Fuwa.

01:18:32.730 --> 01:18:35.990
There's nothing for you to be worried about.

01:18:35.990 --> 01:18:41.380
You've only fulfilled your obligation as an adult living in this society.

01:18:41.380 --> 01:18:47.970
Alvil, the other students that were on the list are coming to this floor now.

01:18:47.970 --> 01:18:51.760
Go welcome them so that they don't get lost.

01:18:51.760 --> 01:18:56.200
Oh, and you're free to kill the unregistered resident.

01:18:59.140 --> 01:19:01.460
Understood.

01:19:02.700 --> 01:19:05.660
If there's anyone who can break my magic,

01:19:05.660 --> 01:19:09.670
it has to be creator of this world's system.

01:19:09.670 --> 01:19:12.550
I stole data from the building's construction company.

01:19:13.010 --> 01:19:14.700
About Ayumi too?

01:19:14.700 --> 01:19:17.160
I figured it out by deduction.

01:19:17.160 --> 01:19:21.530
But that doesn't change the situation in any way.

01:19:22.230 --> 01:19:28.610
Unless we defeat this monster, no place is safe.

01:19:44.840 --> 01:19:48.720
No sound and nothing in sight, huh?

01:19:52.090 --> 01:19:53.430
Mio, you're going too far ahead.

01:19:54.140 --> 01:19:55.450
I'm fine.

01:19:55.450 --> 01:19:59.270
In this robot, a car could hit me, and there wouldn't be a single scratch.

01:20:05.060 --> 01:20:06.070
Mio!

01:20:06.710 --> 01:20:07.610
That guy!

01:20:07.990 --> 01:20:09.890
Let go!

01:20:09.890 --> 01:20:11.270
You—

01:20:11.270 --> 01:20:13.160
I said, let go!

01:20:15.780 --> 01:20:18.360
Hazuki, you stay here.

01:20:18.360 --> 01:20:19.240
Rei Myao-san?

01:20:25.190 --> 01:20:26.170
Let go of Mio!

01:20:31.000 --> 01:20:31.850
Rei Myao-san!

01:20:59.350 --> 01:21:00.220
Myao...

01:21:02.700 --> 01:21:04.010
Rei Myao-san?

01:21:05.930 --> 01:21:06.800
Mio...

01:21:11.210 --> 01:21:12.370
I have to save them...

01:21:13.110 --> 01:21:15.450
I have to save them both.

01:21:26.280 --> 01:21:29.550
You shouldn't touch something like this.

01:21:29.550 --> 01:21:32.160
The valuable material will be damaged.

01:21:37.710 --> 01:21:38.790
I was waiting...

01:21:39.750 --> 01:21:41.770
until your hands were occupied.

01:22:02.530 --> 01:22:03.730
Ayumi?

01:22:03.730 --> 01:22:05.470
I'm glad to see that you're all right.

01:22:06.420 --> 01:22:08.460
I would've been fine by myself.

01:22:11.060 --> 01:22:13.860
I was the only one who needed to come here.

01:22:13.860 --> 01:22:15.810
Me, the killer.

01:22:20.350 --> 01:22:23.840
I feel your body warmth.

01:22:25.510 --> 01:22:29.730
Just like us, warm blood flows in you.

01:22:30.400 --> 01:22:33.210
So, let's all go together.

01:22:33.210 --> 01:22:35.050
Let's put an end to it together.

01:22:41.810 --> 01:22:42.760
Yeah.

01:22:43.310 --> 01:22:44.750
Let's go.

01:22:44.750 --> 01:22:45.660
Mio!

01:22:46.100 --> 01:22:47.330
Rei Myao-san!

01:22:58.280 --> 01:22:59.850
Wow, what is this?

01:22:59.850 --> 01:23:01.830
It's amazing! They're dancing!

01:23:02.140 --> 01:23:04.340
What in the world is this?

01:23:04.340 --> 01:23:08.460
Someone is trying to destroy the rules of this world.

01:23:08.460 --> 01:23:09.290
Who?

01:23:09.540 --> 01:23:12.380
I assume it's Ookami-sama.

01:23:12.380 --> 01:23:13.760
Huh?

01:23:13.760 --> 01:23:18.450
I haven't talked to anyone today.

01:23:20.120 --> 01:23:25.440
On a night like this, a star shoots away.

01:23:26.520 --> 01:23:32.730
Actually, I want to feel like I'm riding a jet coaster.

01:23:33.080 --> 01:23:38.330
While yawning, the TV at midnight...

01:23:38.330 --> 01:23:41.530
A message mixed with a noise came from somewhere.

01:23:41.530 --> 01:23:44.290
I am the past.

01:23:44.290 --> 01:23:51.090
Despite our distance, we can still touch.

01:23:54.120 --> 01:23:57.180
Father, Mother, good night.

01:23:57.180 --> 01:24:06.560
Starting now, I'm going to build a new future.

01:24:08.060 --> 01:24:11.480
From a mysterious star far away,

01:24:11.480 --> 01:24:15.890
A pure power rains down.

01:24:15.890 --> 01:24:19.280
On the way home, I took the long way.

01:24:20.920 --> 01:24:24.240
It's like the day we first kissed.

01:24:24.240 --> 01:24:28.950
A pure power rains down.

01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:33.670
Be closer.

01:24:39.520 --> 01:24:41.640
What's happening?

01:24:41.920 --> 01:24:44.120
Answer me, Administrative Officer Ishida!

01:24:44.120 --> 01:24:46.710
I am about to be taken over.

01:24:47.850 --> 01:24:50.060
I won't let that happen.

01:24:50.060 --> 01:24:51.840
I, me, I...

01:24:51.840 --> 01:24:53.670
It's me. I am Ishida.

01:24:53.670 --> 01:24:54.490
Who?

01:24:54.490 --> 01:25:05.380
I... It's me... Ishida...

01:25:05.380 --> 01:25:06.410
It's me!

01:25:07.630 --> 01:25:08.960
Tsuzuki-san?

01:25:20.040 --> 01:25:22.220
What did you do?

01:25:22.580 --> 01:25:27.560
I put the SVC network, or rather the Society, into a state of chaos.

01:25:27.880 --> 01:25:29.020
Hacking again?

01:25:29.020 --> 01:25:30.980
I wouldn't do such a thing.

01:25:31.220 --> 01:25:32.810
Magic tricks again?

01:25:32.810 --> 01:25:33.940
It's real magic!

01:25:34.200 --> 01:25:35.340
It's illegal.

01:25:38.000 --> 01:25:39.170
Fuwa-san?

01:25:42.280 --> 01:25:44.700
I'm glad you're all okay too.

01:25:45.480 --> 01:25:46.430
Too?

01:25:46.430 --> 01:25:48.580
You mean there are other kids as well?

01:25:48.580 --> 01:25:49.350
Yes.

01:25:49.350 --> 01:25:50.760
They're inside.

01:25:50.760 --> 01:25:52.410
What about that person called Ishida?

01:25:52.410 --> 01:25:54.150
Administrative Officer Ishida?

01:25:54.150 --> 01:25:56.380
We talked through the Monitor, but...

01:25:56.910 --> 01:25:58.420
Through the Monitor, huh?

01:25:58.990 --> 01:26:01.740
Then it has to be in here.

01:26:01.740 --> 01:26:04.370
Does that place have some significance?

01:26:04.370 --> 01:26:06.760
The center of this world.

01:26:06.760 --> 01:26:09.590
In other words, it's where the villain is.

01:26:38.720 --> 01:26:39.840
What is that?

01:26:41.460 --> 01:26:43.110
Administrative Officer Ishida?

01:26:44.480 --> 01:26:45.800
Oh my, oh my.

01:26:46.580 --> 01:26:51.760
If I remember correctly, you are the
counselor of Area 122, Fuwa Shizue-san.

01:26:52.320 --> 01:26:54.830
And her students: Tsuzuki Mio-san...

01:26:54.830 --> 01:26:56.660
Kono Ayumi-san...

01:26:56.660 --> 01:26:59.360
and Makino Hazuki-san.

01:27:01.110 --> 01:27:03.740
You're not in the records.

01:27:04.120 --> 01:27:05.700
You're not Ishida?

01:27:05.700 --> 01:27:06.960
Ishida?

01:27:06.960 --> 01:27:09.510
Oh, Riichiro.

01:27:09.510 --> 01:27:13.810
There was never a person named Ishida Riichiro.

01:27:13.810 --> 01:27:15.420
He was just data.

01:27:16.370 --> 01:27:19.900
He was an illusion that I created.

01:27:19.900 --> 01:27:24.600
I can't go out in public looking like this.
After all, I'm more than a hundred years old.

01:27:24.600 --> 01:27:26.970
I made it look like I'm dead.

01:27:26.970 --> 01:27:29.180
That means you're...

01:27:29.180 --> 01:27:31.380
Suzuki Keitarou.

01:27:32.540 --> 01:27:37.020
I'm just a food hobbyist seeking the ideal taste.

01:27:37.660 --> 01:27:41.980
Long ago, during the war, I used to go to an island in the south.

01:27:42.610 --> 01:27:47.010
I was unable to forget the taste of the meat I ate there to survive.

01:27:47.010 --> 01:27:51.330
After tasting that forbidden food, I became cursed.

01:27:51.330 --> 01:27:57.600
So I started the SVC just to recreate that taste.

01:27:57.600 --> 01:27:59.920
It's become pretty large.

01:27:59.920 --> 01:28:05.340
But only my memory recalls that flavor.

01:28:05.340 --> 01:28:09.640
Because I can never forget that taste, I keep seeking it,

01:28:10.320 --> 01:28:14.470
using all the power and financial resources I have.

01:28:15.110 --> 01:28:18.210
Thank you, Fuwa Shizue-san,

01:28:18.690 --> 01:28:21.780
for guiding these children correctly.

01:28:24.680 --> 01:28:27.750
You are full of curiosity and intelligence,

01:28:27.750 --> 01:28:30.300
but your lifestyle is unhealthy.

01:28:31.530 --> 01:28:34.210
You have anti-social eyes.

01:28:34.210 --> 01:28:37.080
However, your body seems very healthy.

01:28:42.800 --> 01:28:45.130
Your condition is very good.

01:28:45.580 --> 01:28:47.350
I'll have you.

01:28:47.350 --> 01:28:49.340
You will be the ingredient for tonight's dinner.

01:28:49.610 --> 01:28:51.750
You grew up in a completely controlled environment

01:28:51.750 --> 01:28:55.020
and seem to have healthy internal organs.

01:28:56.430 --> 01:28:57.930
No!

01:29:07.530 --> 01:29:11.160
Stabbing people like it's a pat on the shoulder...

01:29:11.560 --> 01:29:13.690
Are you a demon?

01:29:15.100 --> 01:29:17.240
I am the Loups=Garous.

01:29:17.240 --> 01:29:18.910
Just a beast.

01:29:31.930 --> 01:29:36.780
Will you release me from this curse?

01:29:36.780 --> 01:29:38.150
No.

01:29:38.150 --> 01:29:39.450
I'm only killing you.

01:30:04.910 --> 01:30:06.290
Fuwa-san.

01:30:08.150 --> 01:30:10.320
I'm an evil person.

01:30:10.320 --> 01:30:12.380
I've killed someone.

01:30:12.980 --> 01:30:17.490
As an adult who knows everything,
you're the only one who can judge me.

01:30:20.560 --> 01:30:21.850
But I...

01:30:22.500 --> 01:30:25.950
Please save me.

01:30:27.230 --> 01:30:28.400
We are together.

01:30:29.930 --> 01:30:31.670
I'm with you.

01:30:32.220 --> 01:30:34.180
Because you're the same as me, Ayumi.

01:30:35.020 --> 01:30:36.910
You have the same warmth.

01:31:05.410 --> 01:31:07.810
Two months have passed since then.

01:31:08.310 --> 01:31:10.780
The police brought us in for questioning.

01:31:10.780 --> 01:31:13.740
Father scolded me a little too.

01:31:14.610 --> 01:31:18.700
Our regular lives slowly returned.

01:31:19.060 --> 01:31:20.540
It looks like there are no problems.

01:31:20.540 --> 01:31:22.360
That's it for today.

01:31:23.140 --> 01:31:25.190
You still have some time,

01:31:25.190 --> 01:31:26.540
so should we have a chat?

01:31:26.540 --> 01:31:29.060
No, I have practice after this.

01:31:30.060 --> 01:31:31.540
So then...

01:31:31.540 --> 01:31:33.030
excuse me!

01:31:37.830 --> 01:31:39.100
Sorry to make you wait.

01:31:40.060 --> 01:31:40.950
Oh?

01:31:40.950 --> 01:31:41.930
What's wrong?

01:31:41.930 --> 01:31:43.750
Myao is acting spoiled.

01:31:43.750 --> 01:31:45.390
Would you help me persuade her?

01:31:45.990 --> 01:31:49.730
Why do I have to dance with you?

01:31:49.730 --> 01:31:51.610
It's communication.

01:31:51.610 --> 01:31:52.620
Communication, you know?

01:31:52.620 --> 01:31:53.750
I don't need any of that.

01:31:53.750 --> 01:31:55.030
It's necessary.

01:31:55.030 --> 01:31:56.000
Now. With—

01:31:56.000 --> 01:31:56.520
I won't.

01:31:56.520 --> 01:31:56.900
A vigilant—

01:31:56.900 --> 01:31:57.570
I won't!

01:31:57.570 --> 01:31:58.410
Eye!

01:32:06.150 --> 01:32:10.840
In the end, they absolved Ayumi of her crimes.

01:32:12.260 --> 01:32:15.680
The serial killing case was left unsolved.

01:32:15.680 --> 01:32:19.890
Suzuki Keitarou was a person who had died long ago.

01:32:19.890 --> 01:32:22.740
They made it look like he'd never been at the SVC.

01:32:23.800 --> 01:32:30.680
Reasons aside, it's an unchangeable fact that Ayumi killed people.

01:32:32.910 --> 01:32:37.900
We have to face that reality for the rest of our lives.

01:32:39.990 --> 01:32:43.480
And that Ayumi is no longer here.

01:32:48.750 --> 01:32:51.340
But I'm here.

01:32:51.340 --> 01:32:53.480
I'm waiting for Ayumi here.

01:32:55.660 --> 01:32:57.640
I see it too...

01:32:57.640 --> 01:32:59.370
The sky you were watching.

01:33:02.320 --> 01:33:03.300
Hazuki!

01:33:05.150 --> 01:33:06.690
Hurry and come over.

01:33:06.690 --> 01:33:08.930
Myao wants to dance.

01:33:08.930 --> 01:33:11.150
Who ever said that?

01:33:12.000 --> 01:33:14.370
I heard the voice in your heart.

01:33:15.620 --> 01:33:17.070
You two...

01:33:18.320 --> 01:33:19.470
Geez.

01:33:29.020 --> 01:33:31.560
I wasn't able to say it after all.

01:33:31.560 --> 01:33:33.730
I still love you now.

01:33:33.730 --> 01:33:39.550
Good bye, my friend.

01:33:57.380 --> 01:34:06.420
In the sunset, bicycles and
two shadows side by side,

01:34:06.420 --> 01:34:15.590
a cool breeze blows like
summer vacation is ending,

01:34:18.210 --> 01:34:22.530
though we can
meet tomorrow too...

01:34:22.530 --> 01:34:27.050
How strange, I feel so lonely.

01:34:27.050 --> 01:34:36.240
Let's take a longer
path home than usual.

01:34:38.320 --> 01:34:40.910
Just being kind wasn't enough.

01:34:40.910 --> 01:34:43.830
Just being happy was empty.

01:34:43.830 --> 01:34:45.070
Why was that?

01:34:45.070 --> 01:34:48.990
In front of me,
I kept trying to act cool.

01:34:48.990 --> 01:34:51.580
Before summer vacation ends,

01:34:51.580 --> 01:34:54.150
I had something
I wanted to tell you.

01:34:54.150 --> 01:34:57.060
If we touch each other again,

01:34:57.060 --> 01:34:59.300
we can't go back anymore.

01:34:59.300 --> 01:35:01.920
I couldn't say it after all.

01:35:01.920 --> 01:35:04.200
I still love you.

01:35:04.200 --> 01:35:09.450
I'm sorry, my friend.

01:35:19.900 --> 01:35:24.460
Exchanging a kiss at the end,

01:35:24.460 --> 01:35:28.990
your dirty room,

01:35:28.990 --> 01:35:38.090
the memories, and the
half-eaten ice cream is melting.

01:35:40.290 --> 01:35:42.870
Being beside you,
I noticed some things:

01:35:42.870 --> 01:35:45.720
There were things I lost
through repeated memories.

01:35:45.720 --> 01:35:48.310
As I became more of an adult,

01:35:48.310 --> 01:35:53.500
there were things I
didn't want to know about.

01:35:53.500 --> 01:35:57.050
You're my friend.

01:35:57.050 --> 01:36:03.320
Now you're just my friend.

01:36:03.820 --> 01:36:06.430
The sound of fireworks
that bloomed expansively,

01:36:06.430 --> 01:36:09.120
erasing them is just fine.

01:36:09.120 --> 01:36:14.140
The love song of the
two that no one can hear.

01:36:14.140 --> 01:36:16.740
Every time our eyes meet,

01:36:16.740 --> 01:36:19.020
every time our names are called,

01:36:19.020 --> 01:36:21.630
tears flow out.

01:36:21.880 --> 01:36:24.470
Before summer vacation ends,

01:36:24.470 --> 01:36:27.090
there was something
I wanted to tell you.

01:36:27.090 --> 01:36:32.240
If it breaks again, we won't be able to go back anymore.

01:36:32.240 --> 01:36:34.800
I couldn't say it after all.

01:36:34.800 --> 01:36:36.920
I still love you.

01:36:36.920 --> 01:36:42.940
Goodbye, my friend.

01:37:53.020 --> 01:37:56.950
It's said that in the past,
there were beasts called Wolves.

01:37:58.780 --> 01:38:02.520
But the Wolves became extinct.

01:38:02.520 --> 01:38:04.660
That's what they thought.
